        "axis": "Long-context understanding (structure-aware social reasoning over online discussion threads)",
        "definition": "1,462 human-authored, verified four-option multiple-choice items drawn from 94 complete Hacker News, Stack Exchange and Reddit r/ChangeMyView discussions (median about 73K tokens). Items test parent-reply relations, turning points, scoped subtrees, cross-branch contrasts and participant trajectories across six capability surfaces (C1-C6). Items are verified for answerability, option uniqueness and evidence grounding. Responses are parsed to A-D and scored by exact match; benchmark-level results use micro accuracy and capability summaries use the macro mean over C1-C6.",
        "task": "Given a serialized full discussion thread with reply structure, a question and four options, locate the evidence and choose the answer.",
